# llm-cite-digest.baseline -- what every line-cited range in llm/ SAID when
# it was last verified.  Regenerate with:
#     python3 scripts/llm-guard.py --record-digests
#
# A digest proves a range still SAYS what it said -- never that it said what the
# doc CLAIMS.  Recording a WRONG citation makes this file defend the error,
# permanently and silently.  --record-digests is NOT a fix for a red run: open the
# cited file at the cited lines first.
#
# REVIEW the git diff: the trailing excerpt is the first cited line, so a
# citation that has silently drifted onto other code shows up as a changed
# excerpt rather than as an opaque hash.  Fields: doc <TAB> cited-spec <TAB>
# digest <TAB> excerpt.  Keyed WITHOUT the doc's own line number, so
# re-flowing a paragraph does not re-key the file.
